# Secrets — never commit
credentials/
.env
.env.local
.dev.vars
*.json.key

# Node
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
.wrangler/

# Tab dumps taken from the live sheet (contain member data)
tmp/

# Spec drops handed over for integration, not part of the build
gate web page/
gate web page.zip

# Source art, kept out because what the build needs is committed already: the
# 6.9MB torch reel reduces to the two torch-*.webp under web/src/assets, and
# scripts/prepare-torches.mjs only has to be rerun if those are being changed.
# Same bargain for the candle sprite archive, extracted under Assets/.
Assets/torchlightgif.gif
Assets/Animated_skyrim_style_candles.zip

# Hesperides was tried for --display and reverted — it comes apart into
# disconnected strokes at label size (see the note in base.css). Nothing embeds
# it, and this repo is public, so committing the face would redistribute a
# foundry font to no purpose. The reasoning is kept in the comment, not the file.
Assets/HESPD___.TTF
Assets/hesperides.zip

# Agent tooling. `.claude/commands/` and `.claude/skills/` are shared project
# tooling — OpenSpec writes its slash commands and skills there, and they should
# travel with the repo like any other workflow. Only the launch config is local:
# it points at a dev-server preview and means nothing on another machine.
.claude/launch.json
